# Kṣetra Sevakaḥ — Cursor Rules

## Project Context
This is an Android Kotlin application using Jetpack Compose, targeting API 28+ (min) and API 35 (compile).
The app runs entirely on-device AI inference via MLC-LLM. No cloud AI APIs.

## Language & Framework
- **Language:** Kotlin 2.0+ with coroutines & Flow
- **UI:** Jetpack Compose with Material Design 3
- **DI:** Hilt (Dagger)
- **Database:** Room (SQLite)
- **Networking:** None for AI. OkHttp only for Google Drive API.
- **Testing:** JUnit5, Turbine (Flow testing), Mockk, Compose UI testing, Robolectric

## Architecture
- **Pattern:** MVI (Model-View-Intent) with unidirectional data flow
- **Modules:** Feature-based modular structure under `:feature:*`
- **Layers per feature:** `ui/` → `domain/` → `data/`

## Code Conventions
- Every public class/function has KDoc
- ViewModels expose `StateFlow<UiState>` and accept `sealed interface UiEvent`
- Repository interfaces live in `domain/`, implementations in `data/`
- Use `Result<T>` wrapper for all repository return types
- SMS operations must ONLY target number `070936 52065`
- All database operations use Room DAOs — never raw SQL in app code
- Composables: stateless where possible, hoisted state to ViewModel

## File Naming
- ViewModels: `*ViewModel.kt`
- Screens: `*Screen.kt`
- DAOs: `*Dao.kt`
- Entities: `*Entity.kt`
- Repositories: `*Repository.kt` (interface), `*RepositoryImpl.kt` (impl)
- UseCases: `*UseCase.kt`
- Workers: `*Worker.kt`

## Package Structure
```
com.ksetrasevakah/
├── app/                    # Application class, MainActivity, NavGraph
├── core/
│   ├── database/           # Room DB, DAOs, Entities, Migrations
│   ├── sms/                # SmsManager wrapper, BroadcastReceiver
│   ├── ai/                 # MLC-LLM engine wrapper
│   ├── vectorstore/        # FAISS/Chroma local vector store
│   ├── backup/             # Google Drive integration
│   ├── di/                 # Hilt modules
│   └── common/             # Result wrapper, extensions, constants
├── feature/
│   ├── hub/                # Main menu / module launcher
│   ├── pumpiq/
│   │   ├── dashboard/      # Dashboard screen + motor control
│   │   ├── prediction/     # Prediction engine + cards
│   │   └── chat/           # AI Analyst chat interface
│   └── settings/           # Settings & backup screen
└── designsystem/           # Theme, colors, typography, components
```

## Testing Rules
- Every ViewModel must have unit tests
- Every Repository must have unit tests with mocked DAOs
- Every DAO must have instrumented tests with in-memory Room DB
- Compose screens must have UI tests for key interactions
- SMS sending must be tested with mocked SmsManager
- Target: 95% line coverage on `core/` and `domain/` layers
- Target: 85% line coverage on `ui/` layer

## Story Implementation Flow
1. Read the story markdown file completely
2. Implement all files listed in "Files to Create/Modify"
3. Write tests as specified in "Test Requirements"
4. Verify all acceptance criteria pass
5. Move to next story only when current is green

